<!--Render Target — AxisComponents
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.target.render.AxisComponents-->
<render:AxisComponents xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type"
  xmlns:render="com.machineblocks.bml.target.render">

  <baseType>
    core:Block
  </baseType>
  <is>
    One customizer field per axis for a scalar-or-axis union
  </is>
  <documentation>
    One customizer rule. It matches a property union of exactly two named
    alternatives: a scalar type, and AxisXY or AxisXYZ closed on that same
    type.

    Each axis becomes its own variable. The name is the property name plus
    the axis letter, so holeXYZShift becomes holeXYZShiftX, holeXYZShiftY,
    and holeXYZShiftZ. A scalar default is copied onto every axis. An
    authored { x, y } or { x, y, z } fills the fields in that order.

    The hidden variable is hlp_ plus the property name. Its value is the
    array of those fields at full length. The main call passes that hidden
    name. The module fallback stays the serialized property value.

    valueType Boolean makes one checkbox per axis. valueType enum matches
    any enum, so HoleType and Align use the same rows. Each enum field is
    the SCAD token. The enum dropdown comment is attached because the field
    value is one token of that enum.
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <valueType type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        FQN of the scalar alternative, or enum for any enum closed on the same axis.
      </documentation>
    </valueType>
    <axis type="type:Text">
      <documentation>
        FQN of the axis alternative. AxisXY makes two fields.
        AxisXYZ makes three.
      </documentation>
    </axis>
  </properties>
</render:AxisComponents>
